      "description": "Watch York City LFC vs Gillingham highlights and goals from League Two on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 26, 2026. On September 26, 2026 , fans gathered for a high-stakes League Two encounter between York City and Gillingham , where both sides looked to establish early momentum. The atmosphere was electric as the two teams clashed in a game defined by clinical finishing and disciplinary drama. Lightning Start for the Hosts York City began the match with intent, catching the visitors cold almost immediately. In just the 2nd minute, Joe Grey found the top right corner with a clinical right-footed strike following a pinpoint cross from Ollie Pearce . The early breakthrough forced Gillingham to rethink their strategy, but their afternoon went from bad to worse as injuries began to take a toll. Both Will Goodwin and Eli King were forced off in the first half, leading to the early introductions of Zane Albarus and Garath McCleary . Despite the lead, York City will feel they could have been further ahead by the break. The hosts were denied by the woodwork twice in the opening period; first, Alex Newby saw his effort rattle the right post in the 27th minute, and later, Alex Hunt suffered the same fate in the 39th. Gillingham struggled to find their rhythm, managing only sporadic attempts that failed to truly test the home defense before the halftime whistle. Red Card and Clinical Finishing The second half saw the momentum shift decisively in favor of the home side. The turning point arrived in the 70th minute when Zane Albarus , who had already been cautioned, received a second yellow card for a foul on Ollie Pearce . Reduced to ten men, Gillingham found it impossible to contain the waves of pressure. Five minutes later, substitute Jovan Malcolm doubled the lead with a superb strike from outside the box that nestled into the bottom left corner. York City added gloss to the scoreline in the 79th minute. Following a corner, Harry Boyes turned provider for Ollie Pearce , who clinicaly dispatched a left-footed shot into the center of the goal. While Gillingham almost grabbed a consolation through James Brophy , whose 85th-minute effort struck the post, the day belonged entirely to the hosts. They saw out the final minutes with professional ease to secure a dominant victory on home soil."
